A||||5||Dan87GT||Fuel "Pre-Filter"||||5
Z||000000||Dan87GT||11-01-1999||07:13 PM||||I have seen that some people are listing a fuel tank "pre-filter" in some of their part lists, is this replaceable?? Should it be cleaned??||||reg||5
Z||000001||ChadMan||11-01-1999||07:31 PM||||The fuel pick-up tube on the fuel pump has a mesh "sock" over it that strains fuel before the pump pumps it out of the tank.  Maybe that's what they mean by a pre-filter?  If so, it should be replaced along if/when the fuel pump is replaced.<P>I had to have my fuel pump replaced in my old 84 at 125K miles.  My mechanic showed me the sock - it was partially clogged, but looked like it should still provide plenty of flow.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Linx||11-01-1999||11:58 PM||||  <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/Speedway/7039/extract3.jpg">  <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/Speedway/7039/resistor4.JPG">   <BR><p>[This message has been edited by Linx (edited 11-02-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Dan87GT||11-02-1999||07:45 AM||||Thanks for the pictures, can the "sock" be purchased or do I have to buy a new fuel pump?||||reg||6
Z||000004||Linx||11-02-1999||08:44 AM||||The filter is pretty common.  $7 at Autozone, if I remember correctly.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Terrybogin||11-02-1999||08:32 PM||||If you get into it far enough to put in a new sock, replace the pump also. The pump is at least 10 years old and probably seen better days. Just don't get the pump at Advance Auto. I had to put in another very soon because the cheap pump quit pumping. I bit the bullet and bought an AC-Delco. It costed about $50 for the pump and sock at the pontiac dealer.||||reg||1
